49,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A requires staffing we don't have. Candidate C is risky. I prefer D, provided it's not too complex.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"B is a bus corridor, but I'm worried about the lane-priority failures Servas mentioned. I'll go with A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,D seems expensive given the contractor fees and data disputes Jonathan found. A uses existing routes.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A was successful in the past. If we can solve the roster issue, it's a proven win.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"B and C are construction nightmares. A is operational, and D is a bureaucratic mess. I vote A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, if you're worried about D's bureaucracy, A's staffing crisis is just as much of a wall.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, we can't just do nothing. A is a direct response to service needs.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, perhaps the lapsed grant could be leveraged for the initial transition of A?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, we must be bold, but grounded. A has the historical precedent we need.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, I agree the rosters are thin, but it's a manageable problem compared to unrecorded voids in the earth.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I still worry about the crews, but I see the others are leaning toward A. I'll reconsider.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm sticking with A. It's the most straightforward improvement.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'll support A. It avoids the paving rate hikes and the shell contingencies.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Servas,,A is my choice. Let us not forget the success of the previous pilot.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,A is the most logical path forward.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"Very well. If the others are certain, I will vote for A to maintain consensus.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
